    "id": "train-1339",
    "question": "A plumber bought 10 meters of copper and 5 more meters of plastic pipe. If each meter cost $4, how much did the plumber spent on the copper and plastic pipe?",
    "gold": "100",
    "answer": "He bought 10 + 5 = <<10+5=15>>15 meters of plastic pipe.\nThe total meters of the copper and plastic pipe is 10 + 15 = <<10+15=25>>25.\nThe plumber spent $4 x 25 = $<<4*25=100>>100 on copper and plastic pipe.\n#### 100"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total cost of the copper and plastic pipe that the plumber bought, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total length of the copper pipe.\n2. Calculate the total length of the plastic pipe.\n3. Find the total cost of the copper pipe.\n4. Find the total cost of the plastic pipe.\n5. Add the total costs of the copper and plastic pipes to get the final amount spent.\n\nLet's start with the first step:\n\n1. The plumber bought 10 meters of copper pipe.\n2. The plumber also bought 5 more meters of plastic pipe than copper pipe. Therefore, the length of the plastic pipe is:\n   \\[\n   10 + 5 = 15 \\text{ meters}\n   \\]\n3. The cost of each meter of pipe is $4. So, the total cost of the copper pipe is:\n   \\[\n   10 \\text{ meters} \\times 4 \\text{ dollars/meter} = 40 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n4. The total cost of the plastic pipe is:\n   \\[\n   15 \\text{ meters} \\times 4 \\text{ dollars/meter} = 60 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n5. The total amount spent by the plumber is the sum of the costs of the copper and plastic pipes:\n   \\[\n   40 \\text{ dollars} + 60 \\text{ dollars} = 100 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the plumber spent \\(\\boxed{100}\\) dollars on the copper and plastic pipe.",
